<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhang Gui</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">255–314</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhang Gui was a Chinese official appointed governor of Liang province in the far north-west by the Western Jin in 301. Ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuwei">Guzang</a>, he restored order, encouraged learning and welcomed refugees from the wars in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. His family continued to govern the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu-corridor">Hexi Corridor</a> after the fall of Western Jin, forming the Former Liang state.</p></div>
